      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baie-Comeau"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Baie‑Comeau was founded in 1936 when a paper mill was built, and the town was incorporated a year later in 1937.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baie-Comeau"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The 1952 Chutes‑aux‑Outardes hydro‑electric station marked the start of large‑scale power projects on the Manicouagan and Outardes rivers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baie-Comeau"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1959, Baie‑Comeau opened Canada’s largest grain warehouses, a testament to its role in regional agriculture.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baie-Comeau"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Baie‑Comeau is the birthplace of former Canadian prime minister Brian Mulroney in Canada.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
